  "description": "JEYNIO crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C24 H29 Cl3 Dy3 O14 1+,C26 H31 Cl4 Dy3 O13,Cl1 1-,2(C1 H4 O1),1.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.510-3.559 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.61-99.05°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy3(μ3-OH)2(L1)3Cl3(H2O)3][Dy3(μ3-OH)2(L1)3Cl4(CH3OH)(H2O)]Cl·4CH3OH·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
